{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Remember the days of eternity.</b> What did He do to the earlier ones who provoked Him?" "<b>Understand the years of generation after generation.</b> The generation of Enosh, upon whom He flooded the waters of Ocean, and the generation of the Flood, whom He swept away. Another interpretation — you did not set your heart upon what has passed; <b>understand the years of generation after generation</b> — to recognize for the future, that it is in His power to do good to you and bequeath you the days of the Messiah and the World to Come (cf. Sifrei)." "<b>Ask your father.</b> These are the prophets, who are called fathers, as it is said (II Kings 2) of Elijah, ״My father, my father, the chariot of Israel״ (Sifrei)." "<b>Your elders.</b> These are the sages." "<b>And they will tell you.</b> The earlier things."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:09.842351212Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}